message: "If you use, adapt, or teach with this model, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Managing Shared Hospital Capacity for Medical Tourism: Patient Behavior, Bed Sharing, and Hybrid Simulation (simulation model)"
abstract: >-
  A behavior-explicit hybrid agent-based and discrete-event simulation, built in AnyLogic,
  of a multi-specialty international-patient hospital department serving medical tourists and
  local patients from the same beds, specialists and appointment slots. Patient behavior
  (medication adherence, physician switching, channel choice and early abandonment) is part
  of the operational logic. Across 30 hybrid and 36 discrete-event-only randomized-seed
  replications at a bed-constrained configuration, the hybrid model's mean inpatient
  admission waiting time is 14.8 days against 25.8 days in an otherwise identical
  discrete-event-only model; the difference is the combined effect of the patient-behavior
  mechanisms. The model's bed-sharing routine runs in both versions and, as implemented,
  adds no beds (see the README).
